      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Current industry standards typically flag political satire as hate speech when it crosses from mere caricature into content that incites real-world violence, targets protected groups with dehumanizing hatred, or is presented without clear context as fact.\n\nMost major platforms like Meta and X do not automatically censor satire unless it contains actionable threats, harassment against specific individuals, or the false equivalence needed to convince users to commit hate-based actions.\n\nYour policy should prioritize transparency by requiring a clear distinction between editorial content and authentic harm, ensuring your team flags only instances where satire logically leads to actual discrimination rather than just disagreeing with a viewpoint.",
