      "content": "You are correct that major platforms often apply lenient standards for political satire while distinguishing them from genuine hate speech, though their enforcement can appear inconsistent due to evolving public pressure and advertiser contracts. Adopting a guardraled approach that closely mirrors global marketplaces is a strategic necessity, not best practice, as it risks expensive third-party certification requirements and alienates potential creators. Instead of preemptively flagging all satirical content, your policy should utilize a clear, documented framework that differentiates between contextual mockery and dehumanization based on objective behavioral patterns rather than shifting social narratives.",
